{
  "schema_version": "1.0",
  "encounter_id": "00698",
  "segments": [
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0001",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 3.03,
      "end_seconds": 10.85,
      "duration_seconds": 7.82,
      "text": "Morning. I'm here about the dizziness. The room spins, mostly when I roll over in bed."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0002",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 15.24,
      "end_seconds": 19.32,
      "duration_seconds": 4.08,
      "text": "How long has it been going on?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0003",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 22.95,
      "end_seconds": 32.8,
      "duration_seconds": 9.85,
      "text": "Since the ear infection. Maybe three weeks after? Or was it before? I can't say when it started exactly."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0004",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 36.65,
      "end_seconds": 40.31,
      "duration_seconds": 3.66,
      "text": "And how long does each spin last?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0005",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 44.65,
      "end_seconds": 53.41,
      "duration_seconds": 8.76,
      "text": "A minute, perhaps. Then it eases. But I feel off for the rest of the day."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0006",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 57.48,
      "end_seconds": 62.36,
      "duration_seconds": 4.88,
      "text": "Any change in your hearing, or ringing in the ear?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0007",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 66.34,
      "end_seconds": 69.76,
      "duration_seconds": 3.42,
      "text": "No. Hearing's the same. No ringing."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0008",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 74.12,
      "end_seconds": 77.25,
      "duration_seconds": 3.13,
      "text": "What medicines are you taking?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0009",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 81.1,
      "end_seconds": 91.64,
      "duration_seconds": 10.54,
      "text": "Betahistine, 16 mg, three times a day, maybe? The GP started it. And amlodipine, 5 mg once a day."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0010",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 95.92,
      "end_seconds": 102.0,
      "duration_seconds": 6.08,
      "text": "Is the betahistine making a difference, as far as you can tell?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0011",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 105.41,
      "end_seconds": 109.0,
      "duration_seconds": 3.59,
      "text": "Not much. Perhaps a little. ~"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0012",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 112.5,
      "end_seconds": 117.33,
      "duration_seconds": 4.83,
      "text": "Right. Tell me about your health background."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0013",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 121.85,
      "end_seconds": 129.13,
      "duration_seconds": 7.28,
      "text": "Ear infection, left ear, last spring. High blood pressure. And migraines, for years."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0014",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 132.66,
      "end_seconds": 138.04,
      "duration_seconds": 5.38,
      "text": "Do you get any aura or headache with the dizziness? ~"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0015",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 142.14,
      "end_seconds": 145.36,
      "duration_seconds": 3.22,
      "text": "No. Just the spinning. ~"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0016",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 148.48,
      "end_seconds": 160.96,
      "duration_seconds": 12.48,
      "text": "I'm going to hold off on the balance manoeuvres today, because you're still unsteady, and I'd like the specialist to do them properly. ~"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0017",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 164.63,
      "end_seconds": 166.28,
      "duration_seconds": 1.65,
      "text": "Fine. ~"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0018",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 170.01,
      "end_seconds": 182.04,
      "duration_seconds": 12.03,
      "text": "From what you tell me, the spinning when you roll over, lasting a minute, after the ear infection, it fits best with benign positional vertigo."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0019",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 186.4,
      "end_seconds": 189.83,
      "duration_seconds": 3.43,
      "text": "Benign. That sounds mild. ~"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0020",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 193.21,
      "end_seconds": 206.24,
      "duration_seconds": 13.03,
      "text": "It's not dangerous. Tiny crystals in the inner ear have moved into the wrong canal, and the brain misreads the signals. ~"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0021",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 210.18,
      "end_seconds": 212.79,
      "duration_seconds": 2.61,
      "text": "Can it be fixed? ~"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0022",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 216.48,
      "end_seconds": 227.15,
      "duration_seconds": 10.67,
      "text": "Yes, there's a simple manoeuvre that moves the crystals back, and it often works in one session. ~"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0023",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 231.06,
      "end_seconds": 235.09,
      "duration_seconds": 4.03,
      "text": "Good. Does it come back? ~"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0024",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 238.73,
      "end_seconds": 247.83,
      "duration_seconds": 9.1,
      "text": "Sometimes. I'd like to arrange a hearing test as well, to be thorough, given the earlier ear infection."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0025",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 251.9,
      "end_seconds": 253.65,
      "duration_seconds": 1.75,
      "text": "Fine. ~"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0026",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 256.91,
      "end_seconds": 265.78,
      "duration_seconds": 8.87,
      "text": "Until then, get up slowly, avoid sudden head turns, and sleep with your head slightly raised."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0027",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 269.18,
      "end_seconds": 270.63,
      "duration_seconds": 1.45,
      "text": "Right. ~"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0028",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 273.79,
      "end_seconds": 279.93,
      "duration_seconds": 6.14,
      "text": "And no driving if you feel a spin coming on. ~"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0029",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 283.89,
      "end_seconds": 287.9,
      "duration_seconds": 4.01,
      "text": "I'll bear it in mind. ~"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0030",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 292.43,
      "end_seconds": 299.22,
      "duration_seconds": 6.79,
      "text": "I'd like to see you in four weeks, to see how the vertigo is."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0031",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 303.48,
      "end_seconds": 305.96,
      "duration_seconds": 2.48,
      "text": "Four weeks. Thanks. ~"
    }
  ]
}
